unicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "R Controlled Vowels"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When a vowel is followed by an <span class=\"strong\">r</span>, it makes a different sound. These are called r controlled vowels. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "These sounds are as follows:<br> <ul><li>ar sound as in <span class=\"italic\">car, guitar, card, smart</span></li> <li>ir sound as in <span class=\"italic\">birth, girl</span></li> <li>or sound as in <span class=\"italic\">manor, author</span></li> <li>er sound as in <span class=\"italic\">butter, cutter, and mother</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">ir sound</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"girl\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the back of the tongue is bunched high so the sides of the tongue touches the back side teeth (same as the <span class=\\\"italic\\\">r sound</span>)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">ar sound</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"card\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the tongue is set low, inside the bottom teeth, then the sound moves into an <span class=\